><span class="mord mathnormal" style="margin-right:0.0278em;">r</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right:0.2778em;"></span><span class="mrel"><span class="mrel"><span class="mord vbox"><span class="thinbox"><span class="rlap"><span class="strut" style="height:0.8889em;vertical-align:-0.1944em;"></span><span class="inner"><span class="mord"><span class="mrel"></span></span></span><span class="fix"></span></span></span></span></span><span class="mspace nobreak"></span><span class="mrel">=</span></span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right:0.2778em;"></span><span class="mord mathnormal">o</span><span class="mclose">}</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right:0.2778em;"></span><span class="mrel">=</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right:0.2778em;"></span><span class="mord">1501.</span></span></span></span></span><span style="top:-3.1613em;"><span class="pstrut" style="height:3.7513em;"></span><span class="stretchy fbox" style="height:1.7513em;border-style:solid;border-width:0.04em;"></span></span></span><span class="vlist-s">​</span></span><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height:0.59em;"><span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span><p class="Paragraph-kKnbIo" dir="auto"><span>This avoids 204 separate eliminations. One genuinely checked final-rank result, together with the validated closed linear trace, supplies the lower bound at every cut.</span></p><p class="Paragraph-kKnbIo" dir="auto"><span>Inactive dirty owned storage must not be counted as active information. Otherwise the initial rank bound becomes larger than 1501 and this argument no longer proves the desired equality. Legal zero-INIT semantics and use-before-INIT checks are essential.</span></p><h3 class="Heading-Ro3lZr" dir="auto"><span>What this does and does not establish about </span><span data-markdown-copy="inline-code" class="InlineCode-Cddi3Y InlineMarkdownIsolate-QWDV4W" dir="ltr">other_rank</span></h3><p class="Paragraph-kKnbIo" dir="auto"><span>If </span><span data-markdown-copy="inline-code" class="InlineCode-Cddi3Y InlineMarkdownIsolate-QWDV4W" dir="ltr">other_rank</span><span> means </span><strong class="font-semibold"><span>all other live rows</span></strong><span>, the lemma gives its value exactly. The verifier can derive that value and check every stored record against it.</span></p><p class="Paragraph-kKnbIo" dir="auto"><span>If it instead means the rank of </span><strong class="font-semibold"><span>public rows only</span></strong><span>, or the rank of </span><strong class="font-semibold"><span>only the listed certificate providers</span></strong><span>, the lemma does not prove it. The new receipt must name the matrix whose rank is certified. A stored integer with an ambiguous label is not enough.</span></p><p class="Paragraph-kKnbIo" dir="auto"><span>There is a short counterexample to the public-only interpretation. Start with public </span><span data-math-display="false" data-math-source="A=x,B=y"><span class="katex"><span class="katex-mathml"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><semantics><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>x</mi><mo separator="true">,</mo><mi>B</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A=x,B=y</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class="katex-html" aria-hidden="true"><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height:0.6833em;"></span><span class="mord mathnormal">A</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right:0.2778em;"></span><span class="mrel">=</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right:0.2778em;"></span></span><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height:0.8778em;vertical-align:-0.1944em;"></span><span class="mord mathnormal">x</span><span class="mpunct">,</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right:0.1667em;"></span><span class="mord mathnormal" style="margin-right:0.0502em;">B</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right:0.2778em;"></span><span class="mrel">=</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right:0.2778em;"></span></span><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height:0.625em;vertical-align:-0.1944em;"></span><span class="mord mathnormal" style="margin-right:0.0359em;">y</span></span></span></span></span><span>, and zero-initialised owned fields </span><span data-math-display="false" data-math-source="S,T"><span class="katex"><span class="katex-mathml"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><semantics><mrow><mi>S</mi><mo separator="true">,</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S,T</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class="katex-html" aria-hidden="true"><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height:0.8778em;vertical-align:-0.1944em;"></span><span class="mord mathnormal" style="margin-right:0.0576em;">S</span><span class="mpunct">,</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right:0.1667em;"></span><span class="mord mathnormal" style="margin-right:0.1389em;">T</span></span></span></span></span><span>, all coframed. Perform</span></p><span class="Display-XTzqIm" data-math-display="true" data-math-source="S\mathrel{+}=A,\qquad A\mathrel{-}=S,\qquad T\mathrel{+}=B."><span class="katex-display"><span class="katex"><span class="katex-mathml"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" display="block"><semantics><mrow><mi>S</mi><mo>+</mo><mo>=</mo><mi>A</mi><mo separator="true">,</mo><mspace width="2em"></mspace><mi>A</mi><mo>−</mo><mo>=</mo><mi>S</mi><mo separator="true">,</mo><mspace width="2em"></mspace><mi>T</mi><mo>+</mo><mo>=</mo><mi>B</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">.</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S\mathrel{+}=A,\qquad A\mathrel{-}=S,\qquad T\mathrel{+}=B.</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class="katex-html" aria-hidden="true"><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height:0.7667em;vertical-align:-0.0833em;"></span><span class="mord mathnormal" style="margin-right:0.0576em;">S</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right:0.2778em;"></span><span class="mrel"><span class="mord">+</span></span></span><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height:0.3669em;"></span><span class="mrel">=</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right:0.2778em;"></span></span><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height:0.8778em;vertical-align:-0.1944em;"></span><span class="mord mathnormal">A</span><span class="mpunct">,</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right:2em;"></span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right:0.1667em;"></span><span class="mord mathnormal">A</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right:0.2778em;"></span><span class="mrel"><span class="mord">−</span></span></span><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height:0.3669em;"></span><span class="mrel">=</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right:0.2778em;"></span></span><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height:0.8778em;vertical-align:-0.1944em;"></span><span class="mord mathnormal" style="margin-right:0.0576em;">S</span><span class="mpunct">,</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right:2em;"></span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right:0.1667em;"></span><span class="mord mathnormal" style="margin-right:0.1389em;">T</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right:0.2778em;"></span><span class="mrel"><span class="mord">+</span></span></span><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height:0.3669em;"></span><span class="mrel">=</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right:0.2778em;"></span></span><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height:0.6833em;"></span><span class="mord mathnormal" style="margin-right:0.0502em;">B</span><span class="mord">.</span></span></span></span></span></span><p class="Paragraph-kKnbIo" dir="auto"><span>The state is now</span></p><span class="Display-XTzqIm" data-math-display="true" data-math-source="A=0,\quad B=y,\quad S=x,\quad T=y."><span class="katex-display"><span class="katex"><span class="katex-mathml"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" display="block"><semantics>