04</span></strong><span> preparation. The prior 167-to-180 adaptation is not interchangeable. Preserve exact before/after bytes, source and candidate hashes, nested input bindings, the helper hash, and fresh native-to-signed receipt identities.</span></p><p class="Paragraph-kKnbIo" dir="auto"><span>Likewise, derive the actual source-versus-7481 and candidate-versus-7481 pair sets and their required union. Neither the old 964 count nor the source’s reported 1,075 count can replace that derivation. Require exact inventory coverage, nonempty expected sets, contiguous catalogue indices, all 104 bindings, all 58 outer gates, and 17 actual calls.</span></p><p class="Paragraph-kKnbIo" dir="auto"><span>The source’s unrerun final launcher remains an input/qualification risk. Git-blob authentication does not discharge it. The candidate must pass the controlled current native and signed chain, including the complete source resource branch used for comparison. Preserve the explicit distinction if a separate source catalogue is not rerun.</span></p><h2 class="Heading-Ro3lZr" dir="auto"><span>6. Smallest decisive first gate and stopping rule</span></h2><p class="Paragraph-kKnbIo" dir="auto"><span>The first gate should now be simpler than the old rank-one gate.</span></p><ol class="List-kOVW5V OrderedList-XsMUSX" dir="auto" start="1"><li class="ListItem-ncLgmg" style="--fade-delay: 0ms;"><span>Authenticate the current word and five edit records, and recheck complete typed incidence.</span></li><li class="ListItem-ncLgmg" style="--fade-delay: 0ms;"><span>Prove equality of the normalised scalar stream and validate all changed coframes, routes, and canonical-map bindings.</span></li><li class="ListItem-ncLgmg" style="--fade-delay: 0ms;"><span>Perform the paired arbitrary-entrance replay, requiring zero exact difference at every matched normalised observation, all 204 pre-CLEAR rows, and every required endpoint.</span></li><li class="ListItem-ncLgmg" style="--fade-delay: 0ms;"><span>C